# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the Live tests:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=ninjam/live/tests/tsan.supp ./live_client_test
#
# AOO's lock-free free lists (Treiber stacks with tagged heads) read the
# head node's 'next' field while another thread may pop that node and
# reuse its memory; the compare-exchange that follows then fails because
# the tag changed, and the value read is thrown away. rt_memory_pool.hpp
# says so ("Technically, this is UB, but we don't care because the CAS loop
# will fail anyway"). To TSan it is a data race, reported from wherever the
# memory is used next (an event, a queue node, a data frame).
race:aoo::detail::free_list::pop
race:aoo::data_frame_allocator::allocate
